# tools/deploy — the box needs FOUR env files at ~/herkules (none of them committed).
# This one file documents all four; copy each block into its own file. They cannot ship as
# four .example files because the repository's .gitignore keeps `.env.*` out of git and only
# un-ignores the exact name `.env.example`.
#
#   .env         compose interpolation only. Compose reads it for every ${VAR} in
#                docker-compose.yml; nothing reaches a container from here unless
#                docker-compose.yml names it in an explicit `environment:` entry.
#   .env.auth    the auth container's own environment (`env_file: .env.auth`).
#   .env.bot     the bbs-bot container's Feishu credentials (`env_file: .env.bot`).
#   .env.backup  the backup container's own environment (`env_file: .env.backup`).
#
# The split keeps Feishu, auth, browser-cookie, and R2 credentials in only the containers that
# use them.
#
# BBS_ORIGIN and BBS_CLIENT_SECRET are in .env *and* .env.auth, with the same value in both:
# compose interpolates them into the bbs container, and auth reads them to seed the
# confidential `bbs` client.

# ═══ .env ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── where ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caddy site address: the bare hostname in production (required Origin CA certificate), http://localhost:3000 in dev.
SITE_ADDRESS=herkules.dev
# Server-owned PEM files, required in production; never put certificate/key contents here.
# The laptop Compose overlay does not mount or require these files.
ORIGIN_CERT_FILE=/etc/herkules-tls/origin.pem
ORIGIN_KEY_FILE=/etc/herkules-tls/origin.key
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://herkules.dev
# apps/bbs's own site: bbs.herkules.dev in production, http://localhost:3003 in dev.
BBS_SITE_ADDRESS=bbs.herkules.dev
# Images built by .github/workflows/images.yml — including the edge caddy, which carries
# services/web's SPA. Dev builds locally and ignores the registry.
# Local Compose builds still require image names. Production ignores these values because the
# active OCI release supplies immutable tag@digest references through images.env.
AUTH_IMAGE_REF=herkules-auth:local
BBS_IMAGE_REF=herkules-bbs:local
CADDY_IMAGE_REF=herkules-caddy:local
BACKUP_IMAGE_REF=herkules-backup:local

# ── postgres ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Interpolated into auth's and bbs's DATABASE_URL and into backup's PGPASSWORD.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ── apps/bbs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This app's origin (cookies, OAuth redirect URI, og:url). Repeat it in .env.auth.
BBS_ORIGIN=https://bbs.herkules.dev
# The confidential `bbs` client's secret. Repeat it in .env.auth. openssl rand -base64 48
BBS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Seals bbs's browser session cookie (>= 32 chars; rotating it signs every browser out).
# bbs only — auth never sees it. openssl rand -base64 48
BBS_COOKIE_SECRET=

# ── monitoring (README "Monitoring") ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare-proxied records for both, with SSL/TLS set to Full (strict).
STATUS_HOST=status.herkules.dev
OPS_HOST=ops.herkules.dev
# The hub's public key for the box's own agent: shown in the hub's "Add system" dialog. The
# hub image is distroless and stores only the private key, so from the box derive it with
#   docker run --rm -v herkules_beszel_data:/d:ro alpine:3.23 sh -c \
#     'apk add -q openssh-keygen && cp /d/id_ed25519 /tmp/k && chmod 600 /tmp/k && ssh-keygen -y -f /tmp/k'
# Leave empty on the very first boot (the agent restart-loops harmlessly); fill in and
# `docker compose up -d beszel-agent`.
BESZEL_KEY=
# Shared secret between backup.sh and the "Backups" row on the status page. openssl rand -hex 24
GATUS_BACKUP_TOKEN=
# Optional dead-man ping from the hub (Better Stack "heartbeat" URL). Empty = off.
BESZEL_HEARTBEAT_URL=

# ═══ .env.auth ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN, DATABASE_URL, TRUSTED_PROXIES and PORT reach auth through
# docker-compose.yml's `environment:` block, so they do not belong in this file.
#
# # openssl rand -base64 48
# AUTH_SECRET=
# # GitHub OAuth app (one per environment). Callback URL: ${PUBLIC_ORIGIN}/auth/callback/github
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# # The organization whose active members are admitted (the app needs read:org, which it requests itself).
# GITHUB_ORG=
# # Seed admins by GitHub login, comma-separated. Promotes at boot and first login; never demotes.
# ADMIN_GITHUB_LOGINS=
# NODE_ENV=production
# # Client ID Metadata Documents: leave off until the auth container can fetch documents from
# # claude.ai/chatgpt.com (docs/auth.md). Optional CIMD_ALLOWED_ORIGINS narrows which origins are fetched.
# CIMD_ENABLED=false
# # Both or neither: auth seeds the confidential `bbs` client from these two and the bbs
# # container presents the same secret. Copy both verbatim from .env.
# BBS_ORIGIN=https://bbs.herkules.dev
# BBS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# # Both or neither: auth seeds the confidential OIDC client `beszel` for the hub at
# # https://${OPS_HOST}; paste the secret into the hub's OIDC provider settings (README).
# OPS_ORIGIN=https://ops.herkules.dev
# # openssl rand -base64 48
# BESZEL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ═══ .env.bot ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Create an internal self-built app, enable its bot, choose WebSocket (长连接) delivery, subscribe
# to the im.message.receive_v1 and application.bot.menu_v6 events and the card.action.trigger
# callback, publish it to the tenant, and add it to the announcement group. Optional bot menu
# (机器人菜单): one item per command with event_key = the command name (search, latest, status, help).
# FEISHU_APP_ID=cli_...
# FEISHU_APP_SECRET=
# The group chat_id (oc_...), fixed permanently on the bot's first successful activation.
# FEISHU_ANNOUNCEMENT_CHAT_ID=oc_...
# SEARCH_INDEX=trgm

# ═══ .env.backup ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PGHOST, PGUSER, PGPASSWORD and DATABASES reach backup through `environment:`.
#
# R2_BUCKET=
# R2_PREFIX=herkules
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=30
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_TYPE=s3
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_PROVIDER=Cloudflare
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_ACL=private
# Cloudflare Object Read & Write tokens may fail uploads unless rclone skips its bucket probe.
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_NO_CHECK_BUCKET=true

# Optional Cloudflare Access OIDC client (auth environment / .env.auth)
CLOUDFLARE_TEAM_NAME=
CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_SECRET=
